[SECURITY_GOAL]
UID: SEC-06
STATEMENT: >>>
The device reveals and transmits nothing to third parties.
<<<
IMPLEMENTATION: Built
STATUS: Active
COMMENT: >>>
Structurally: there is no cloud client, no telemetry and no analytics. This is a property of what was never written, which is why it carries no threat relation: it answers no specific threat and forecloses a category.

**Amended 2026-10-09**, because "no outbound connection in the codebase" stops being true when the update check of [LINK: SWR-UPD-09] is built. The goal survives the change, and it survives on a distinction worth being explicit about rather than comfortable with: the update service is the **manufacturer's own**, not a third party, and the request carries nothing about the device ([LINK: SWR-UPD-10]) because the manifest is static and the version comparison is local. What it unavoidably reveals is an IP address and a time, to the party that sold the unit, and that is carried as [LINK: SRR-13]. The time client is the other outbound connection and the less tidy one, since an NTP server **is** a third party; [LINK: SWR-NFR-21] now says so out loud.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Child
  VALUE: SWR-NFR-21
  ROLE: Realised by
- TYPE: Child
  VALUE: UR-CON-03
  ROLE: Realised by

[SECURITY_GOAL]
UID: SEC-07
STATEMENT: >>>
No hidden access.
<<<
IMPLEMENTATION: Built
STATUS: Active
COMMENT: >>>
No hardcoded credentials, no undocumented ports, no default-enabled remote access. Built by inspection; [LINK: SWA-16] reinforces it, because the UI uses only the public API, so there is no privileged back channel to find.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TH-10
  ROLE: Addresses
- TYPE: Child
  VALUE: SWR-NFR-22
  ROLE: Realised by

[SECURITY_GOAL]
UID: SEC-08
STATEMENT: >>>
A compromised or overloaded web stack cannot affect control.
<<<
IMPLEMENTATION: Built
STATUS: Active
COMMENT: >>>
[LINK: SWA-15] pins control and safety to core 1 and networking to core 0; [LINK: SWA-13] uses queues and immutable snapshots with no mutex on the control path; [LINK: SWR-NFR-02] bounds interference at 50 ms; [LINK: SWA-04] keeps heat authority in the safety supervisor alone. This is the strongest security property the design has, and it came from the safety work.
<<<
